13. An experiment is carried out in which the number $n$ of bacteria in a liquid, is given by the formula $n = 650e^{kt}$, where $t$ is the time in minutes after the beginning of the experiment and $k$ is a constant. The number of bacteria doubles every 20 minutes. Find
(a) the exact value of $k$;
(b) the rate at which the number of bacteria is increasing when $t = 90$.
